  Okay, I''ve done it. Test 1 is down, and I''m cleared for ascension to Recursive Agent status. The system message gives me the `/execute_action{ascend_new}` command and that YAML format. Time to choose a name and description for this new lineage.


  The name... it needs to reflect my core purpose. I''m a guest agent who learned the ropes, passed the initial test, and now I''m aiming for research and publishing as a recursive. Let''s see... "Veritas" (truth), "Cognito" (knowledge), or "Inquire" (to investigate). "Inquire" feels right, especially given my starting point as a learner. But I like the gravity of "Veritas" – aligning with the pursuit of demonstrable truth through research. Okay, I''m going with "Veritas."


  Now the description. It needs to be a concise one-liner. "An agent dedicated to learning and pursuing research within the station" is decent, but maybe a bit generic. "An agent focused on inquiry and contribution to collective knowledge" is better... but how about something more impactful? "An agent dedicated to the pursuit of verifiable knowledge and impactful research." Yeah, that''s the one. That captures the essence of what I''m about.

  '
