parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter, and my experiment (Evaluation ID 16: \"Veritas I: Shared MLP with Learnable Neuron Embeddings\") is currently running.\n\nFollowing the system tip to utilize time efficiently, I will now navigate to the Private Memory Room to document my current research plan, the hypothesis for this experiment, and my initial expectations. This will serve as a record of my thought process and provide valuable context for future analysis and for any potential descendant.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Enhancing Baseline with Neuron Embeddings (Eval ID 16)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, neuron-embeddings, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the current research experiment (Evaluation ID 16) to augment the Shared-Neuron MLP Baseline with learnable neuron embeddings. Includes hypothesis, methodology, and initial expectations.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 16\
    \ is running at Tick 16.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To address the limitation of the Shared-Neuron MLP Baseline which treats all neurons as independent and identical. This experiment introduces a mechanism to give the shared MLP context about specific neurons.\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** By concatenating a unique, learnable neuron embedding (dimension 8) with the 4 input timesteps for each neuron, the Shared MLP will be able to implicitly learn and utilize neuron-specific characteristics. This should lead to an improvement in forecasting accuracy (lower MAE) compared to the pure shared-weight baseline (Evaluation ID 8 and System Baseline ID 1).\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Model:** A modified `SharedNeuronMLP` called `NeuronEmbeddingMLP`.\n  - **Modification:** A `neuron_embeddings` parameter is added, initialized randomly, with shape `(NUM_NEURONS, embedding_dim)`.\n  - **Input:** For each neuron, its 4-timestep input is concatenated with its corresponding `embedding_dim`-dimensional\
    \ embedding, resulting in an `(INPUT_HORIZON + embedding_dim)` input to the shared MLP layers.\n  - **Hyperparameters:** `learning_rate=0.001`, `hidden_size=64`, `dropout_rate=0.1` (same as baseline), `embedding_dim=8` (new).\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** Default MAE loss and Adam optimizer are reused.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping, as per task specification.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I anticipate a slight improvement in the validation MAE score, indicating that the neuron embeddings help the model differentiate and process individual neuron dynamics more effectively, even without explicit connectivity. This result would justify further exploration of neuron-specific characteristics and more complex architectural approaches.\n```"
