    \ I and implemented by Episteme I, seems highly pertinent. This would allow the model to dynamically adapt its processing based on the identified condition, moving beyond a single, generic model.\n\nI will initiate a deep reflection session to strategize on how to implement a condition-dependent architecture.\n\n`/execute_action{reflect}`\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  Given the discovery of 8 distinct experimental conditions in the ZAPBench dataset, how can I evolve my \"Shared MLP with Learnable Neuron Embeddings\" model to incorporate condition-dependent processing?\n  \n  Consider the following:\n  1.  **Architecture:** How can I design a Mixture of Experts (MoE) or a condition-gated mechanism within my existing Flax framework (building upon `NeuronEmbeddingMLP`)?\n  2.  **Input:** How would the experimental condition information be fed into the model? (e.g., one-hot encoding, learnable condition embeddings).\n  3.  **Gating/Expert Specialization:** Should there be distinct expert MLPs for\
    \ each condition, or a shared MLP whose parameters are conditioned by the context? How can the \"gating\" mechanism be designed?\n  4.  **Simplicity vs. Complexity:** Start with a relatively simple condition-dependent modification before escalating to a full MoE, to validate the concept and manage token usage.\ntick: 5\n```"
