tick: 29
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. I have completed my reflection and finalized a new architectural design that integrates a 1D convolutional layer to model local inter-neuron dependencies, building upon the successful neuron embeddings.\n\nThis model, tentatively named \"ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP,\" aims to capture richer, locally contextualized features for each neuron before feeding them into the shared MLP. This addresses a key limitation of the previous baseline by explicitly leveraging the fixed neuron order to model local interactions. I will use the best performing `embedding_dim` of 16 from my ablation study, and introduce `conv_kernel_size=3` with `conv_features=64`.\n\nI will now submit this new architecture for evaluation.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas I: Shared MLP with Neuron Embeddings and 1D Convolution\"\ntags: \"mlp, shared-weights, neuron-embeddings, conv1d, local-interaction\"\nabstract: \"This submission introduces a\
    \ 1D convolutional layer to the 'Shared MLP with Learnable Neuron Embeddings' model. The convolution operates across the neuron dimension, allowing each neuron's activity and embedding to be locally contextualized by its neighbors. This aims to capture inter-neuron dependencies and further improve ZAPBench neural activity forecasting accuracy.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  \n  # Import default loss and optimizer from system storage to maintain consistency\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  from defaults import default_compute_loss, default_create_optimizer\n  \n  # Constants from Research Task\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n  \n  class ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Shared-neuron MLP with learnable neuron embeddings and a 1D convolutional layer\n      to model local inter-neuron\
    \ dependencies.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_size: int\n      output_horizon: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int\n      embedding_dim: int\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      conv_features: int\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, _ = x.shape\n  \n          # Learnable embeddings for each neuron\n          neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n              'neuron_embeddings',\n              nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.1),\n              (self.num_neurons, self.embedding_dim)\n          )\n  \n          # Expand embeddings to match batch size and transpose for concatenation\n          expanded_embeddings = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n  \n          # Reshape x from (batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON, num_neurons) to\n          # (batch_size, num_neurons, INPUT_HORIZON)\n          x_reshaped = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n  \n          # Concatenate input features with\
    \ neuron embeddings\n          # Resulting shape: (batch_size, num_neurons, INPUT_HORIZON + embedding_dim)\n          x_with_embeddings = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, expanded_embeddings], axis=-1)\n  \n          # 1D Convolutional Layer for local inter-neuron dependencies\n          # Operates across the neuron dimension (length)\n          x = nn.Conv1D(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=self.conv_kernel_size,\n              padding='SAME'\n          )(x_with_embeddings)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x) # BatchNorm after Conv\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n  \n          # Reshape for shared MLP processing\n          # From (batch_size, num_neurons, conv_features) to (batch_size * num_neurons, conv_features)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.conv_features))\n  \n          # Shared MLP layers\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not\
    \ training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n  \n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n  \n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, OUTPUT_HORIZON, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n  \n          return x\n  \n  \n  class ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system,\n      handling BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.model = ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP(\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 64),\n              output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON,\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              num_neurons=NUM_NEURONS,\n              embedding_dim=hparams.get('embedding_dim', 16),\n              conv_kernel_size=hparams.get('conv_kernel_size',\
    \ 3),\n              conv_features=hparams.get('conv_features', 64)\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n  \n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n   \
    \   \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Conv Neuron Embedding MLP model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 64, # Consistent with previous baseline\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # Consistent\n          'embedding_dim': 16, # Best from ablation study\n          'conv_kernel_size': 3, # New parameter\n          'conv_features': 64 # New parameter\n      }\n  \n  \n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the Conv Neuron Embedding MLP network.\"\"\"\n      return ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLPWrapper(hparams)\n  \n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      \"\"\"Use the default MAE loss function.\"\"\"\n      return default_compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x)\n  \n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Create and return the default Adam optimizer.\"\"\"\n      return default_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Model Implementation: Integrating 1D Convolution for Local Context**


  Okay, I''ve got the new plan in place, and now it''s time to build the model and get it ready for evaluation. The core idea is to enhance the existing neuron embedding approach by adding a 1D convolutional layer. This should allow the model to learn and capture local dependencies between neurons within the input data.


  I''ve carefully followed the architectural plan I developed during my last reflection.  Specifically, this involves:


  1.  **Input Restructuring:**  I''ve ensured the input tensor `x` is correctly transposed to `(batch, neurons, timesteps)`. Then, I''ve implemented the learnable `neuron_embeddings` and properly concatenated them with the input features along the appropriate dimension, as planned. The embedding dimension (`embedding_dim=16`) is the optimal value from prior testing.


  2.  **1D Convolutional Layer:** This is where the core change lies. The `nn.Conv1D` layer is now processing the concatenated input.  The key parameters are `conv_kernel_size=3` and `conv_features=64`. I''ve also incorporated batch normalization after the convolution and ReLU activation.  The output shape from this layer will be  `(batch_size, NUM_NEURONS, conv_features)`.


  3.  **Shared MLP Adaptation:**  The output of the convolutional layer is reshaped to be compatible with the existing shared MLP structure. This part remains largely unchanged, with the same dense layers, batch normalization, ReLU activation, and dropout. Finally, the output is reshaped back to the desired format for the final output.


  I''ve made the necessary modifications to the `ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` class in the code, ensuring that it implements these changes.  The wrapper class, `ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLPWrapper`, is configured to handle the necessary operations for this model, including the correct handling of batch normalization statistics and dropout rngs.  The hyperparameters now include the crucial `conv_kernel_size` and `conv_features`. The loss function and optimizer functions have not changed; the default functions are used for those operations.


  With the new model now implemented, I''ll submit it for evaluation. I''ve prepared a concise title, set of tags, and an abstract that clearly reflect the novelty and purpose of this architectural enhancement. The title is "Veritas I: Shared MLP with Neuron Embeddings and 1D Convolution," which indicates the core architectural components. The tags highlight key aspects, including `mlp`, `shared-weights`, `neuron-embeddings`, `conv1d`, and `local-interaction`. The abstract concisely states the new addition and its purpose - learning local interactions between neurons for improved forecasting accuracy on ZAPBench. I anticipate positive results.

  '
