- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 45 (\"Veritas I: Shared MLP with Neuron Embeddings and 1D Convolution\"), is running.\n\nTo make efficient use of this waiting period and maintain thorough research records, I will now navigate to the Private Memory Room. There, I will create a new capsule documenting the details of this new architectural approach, including its hypothesis and anticipated outcomes. This ensures that my progress and thought process are well-documented for my lineage.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP (Eval ID 45)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, conv1d, neuron-embeddings, local-interaction, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the current experiment (Evaluation ID 45) introducing a 1D convolutional layer for local inter-neuron dependency modeling. Includes hypothesis, methodology, and expected results.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current\
    \ Status:** Evaluation ID 45 is running at Tick 30.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To move beyond the independent neuron assumption by introducing explicit local inter-neuron dependencies. This is achieved by adding a 1D convolutional layer that operates across the neuron dimension, combining each neuron's activity with its learned embedding and local neighbors' context.\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** Incorporating local spatial dependencies via a 1D convolutional layer will further improve forecasting accuracy compared to models using only neuron embeddings. This addresses a key limitation of the baseline model identified in the research task.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Model:** `ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP`, an extension of the previous `NeuronEmbeddingMLP`.\n  - **Modification:** A `nn.Conv1D` layer is added after concatenating raw input features and neuron embeddings. This layer (`conv_kernel_size=3`, `conv_features=64`) processes features across the `NUM_NEURONS` dimension. It's followed by\
    \ BatchNorm and ReLU.\n  - **Input to Shared MLP:** The output of the Conv1D block is then flattened and fed into the original shared MLP.\n  - **Hyperparameters:** `learning_rate=0.001`, `hidden_size=64`, `dropout_rate=0.1` (consistent), `embedding_dim=16` (best from ablation), `conv_kernel_size=3`, `conv_features=64` (new).\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** Default MAE loss and Adam optimizer are reused.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I anticipate a further improvement in the validation MAE score, pushing past the -0.028735 achieved with `embedding_dim=16`. This would validate the hypothesis that local inter-neuron dependencies, even when modeled simply with 1D convolutions, contribute positively to the forecasting task. This step also lays groundwork for more complex spatial or graph-based models in the future.\n```"
