parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. My corrected experiment, Evaluation ID 52 (\"Veritas I: Shared MLP with Neuron Embeddings and 1D Convolution (Corrected)\"), is currently running.\n\nTo maintain thorough records and utilize this waiting period efficiently, I will navigate to the Private Memory Room. There, I will create a new capsule to document the details of this resubmitted experiment, explicitly noting the bug fix and reiterating its hypothesis and expected outcomes.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP (Corrected) (Eval ID 52)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, conv, neuron-embeddings, local-interaction, bugfix, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation for the resubmitted experiment (Evaluation ID 52), which corrects a typo in the previous attempt (Eval ID 45). Details the architecture combining neuron embeddings with a 1D convolutional layer for local inter-neuron dependency modeling.\
    \ Includes hypothesis, methodology, and expected results.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 52 is running at Tick 33. This is a resubmission after correcting a `flax.linen.Conv1D` to `flax.linen.Conv` typo in Evaluation ID 45.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To move beyond the independent neuron assumption by introducing explicit local inter-neuron dependencies. This is achieved by adding a 1D convolutional layer that operates across the neuron dimension, combining each neuron's activity with its learned embedding and local neighbors' context.\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** Incorporating local spatial dependencies via a 1D convolutional layer will further improve forecasting accuracy compared to models using only neuron embeddings (Eval ID 31: -0.028735). This addresses a key limitation of the baseline model identified in the research task.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Model:** `ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP`, an extension of the previous `NeuronEmbeddingMLP`.\n  - **Modification:**\
    \ A `nn.Conv` layer is added after concatenating raw input features and neuron embeddings. This layer (`conv_kernel_size=3`, `conv_features=64`) processes features across the `NUM_NEURONS` dimension. It's followed by BatchNorm and ReLU.\n  - **Input to Shared MLP:** The output of the Conv block is then flattened and fed into the original shared MLP.\n  - **Hyperparameters:** `learning_rate=0.001`, `hidden_size=64`, `dropout_rate=0.1` (consistent), `embedding_dim=16` (best from ablation), `conv_kernel_size=3`, `conv_features=64` (new).\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** Default MAE loss and Adam optimizer are reused.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I anticipate a further improvement in the validation MAE score beyond -0.028735, validating that local inter-neuron dependencies, even when modeled simply with 1D convolutions, contribute positively to the forecasting task.\n```"
