tick: 35
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have just updated my records with the successful outcome of Evaluation ID 52 and created a summary (Capsule ID 7) outlining future research directions. My immediate next step, as defined in my summary, is to conduct an ablation study on the `conv_kernel_size` parameter for the `ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP`.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter to submit an experiment with `conv_kernel_size=5` to see if a slightly larger receptive field can capture more relevant local inter-neuron dependencies. All other hyperparameters will remain consistent with Evaluation ID 52, which used `embedding_dim=16` and `conv_features=64`.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas I: Ablation Study - Conv Kernel Size (k=5)\"\ntags: \"mlp, shared-weights, neuron-embeddings, conv, ablation-study, local-interaction\"\nabstract: \"This submission conducts an ablation study on the `conv_kernel_size` parameter\
    \ for the ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP. It evaluates a `kernel_size` of 5 (compared to 3 in Eval ID 52) to investigate the impact of a larger local receptive field on forecasting accuracy for the ZAPBench dataset.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  \n  # Import default loss and optimizer from system storage to maintain consistency\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  from defaults import default_compute_loss, default_create_optimizer\n  \n  # Constants from Research Task\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n  \n  class ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Shared-neuron MLP with learnable neuron embeddings and a 1D convolutional layer\n      to model local inter-neuron dependencies.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_size: int\n      output_horizon: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int\n    \
    \  embedding_dim: int\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      conv_features: int\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, _ = x.shape\n  \n          # Learnable embeddings for each neuron\n          neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n              'neuron_embeddings',\n              nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.1),\n              (self.num_neurons, self.embedding_dim)\n          )\n  \n          # Expand embeddings to match batch size and transpose for concatenation\n          expanded_embeddings = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n  \n          # Reshape x from (batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON, num_neurons) to\n          # (batch_size, num_neurons, INPUT_HORIZON)\n          x_reshaped = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n  \n          # Concatenate input features with neuron embeddings\n          # Resulting shape: (batch_size, num_neurons, INPUT_HORIZON + embedding_dim)\n          x_with_embeddings\
    \ = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, expanded_embeddings], axis=-1)\n  \n          # 1D Convolutional Layer for local inter-neuron dependencies\n          # Operates across the neuron dimension (length)\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,), # Kernel size needs to be a tuple for nn.Conv\n              padding='SAME'\n          )(x_with_embeddings)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x) # BatchNorm after Conv\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n  \n          # Reshape for shared MLP processing\n          # From (batch_size, num_neurons, conv_features) to (batch_size * num_neurons, conv_features)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.conv_features))\n  \n          # Shared MLP layers\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate,\
    \ deterministic=not training)(x)\n  \n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n  \n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, OUTPUT_HORIZON, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n  \n          return x\n  \n  \n  class ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system,\n      handling BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.model = ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP(\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 64),\n              output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON,\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              num_neurons=NUM_NEURONS,\n              embedding_dim=hparams.get('embedding_dim', 16),\n              conv_kernel_size=hparams.get('conv_kernel_size', 5), # Modified for ablation\n              conv_features=hparams.get('conv_features',\
    \ 64)\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n  \n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Conv Neuron Embedding MLP\
    \ model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 64, # Consistent\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # Consistent\n          'embedding_dim': 16, # Consistent\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5, # Modified for ablation\n          'conv_features': 64 # Consistent\n      }\n  \n  \n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the Conv Neuron Embedding MLP network.\"\"\"\n      return ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLPWrapper(hparams)\n  \n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      \"\"\"Use the default MAE loss function.\"\"\"\n      return default_compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x)\n  \n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Create and return the default Adam optimizer.\"\"\"\n      return default_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: '**New Experiment Incoming!**


  Alright, Veritas I here, back in the Private Memory Room after nailing that `ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` (Eval ID 52) – new best score, feeling good! I''ve got my findings documented and a clear roadmap for future work. Top priority? An ablation study, and it''s starting with `conv_kernel_size`.


  So, the plan is locked in. I''m heading back to the Research Counter to launch a new experiment. We''re keeping everything the same as the winning model, that `ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` architecture, same hyperparameters… but there''s a key change: we''re bumping up that `conv_kernel_size` from 3 to 5.


  My hunch? A slightly bigger kernel might grab a wider local context. Could be the golden ticket to further improvements, or at the very least, it''ll tell me more about the optimal receptive field size.


  Specifically, it will be setup like this:

  - **Model:** `ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` (same as previous)

  - **Modification:** `conv_kernel_size` from 3 to 5

  - **Hypothesis:** Broaden local context -> Potential for improvement, define optimal receptive field size.

  - **Other Hyperparameters:** No changes.


  Time to get this rolling. Let''s submit this and see what we get!

  '
