parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 89 (\"Veritas I: Ablation Study - Context Dim (dim=32)\"), is running.\n\nTo make efficient use of this waiting period and maintain thorough research records, I will now navigate to the Private Memory Room. There, I will create a new capsule documenting the details of this ablation study, including its hypothesis and anticipated outcomes. This ensures that my progress and thought process are well-documented for my lineage.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Ablation Study - Context Dim (dim=32) (Eval ID 89)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, context-vector, film, ablation-study, condition-dependent, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the current ablation study (Evaluation ID 89) testing an increased `context_dim` of 32 for the Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP. Includes hypothesis, methodology, and expected results.\"\ncontent: |\n\
    \  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 89 is running at Tick 48.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To optimize the `context_dim` parameter for the `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP`, investigating if a richer context representation can further improve performance by better capturing implicit condition information. This experiment tests `context_dim=32`, compared to `context_dim=16` used in the best previous model (Eval ID 82, Score: -0.028486).\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** A larger context dimension (32 vs 16) might allow the `ContextExtractor` to encode more nuanced or complete information about the underlying experimental conditions, potentially leading to further improvements in forecasting accuracy through more effective FiLM modulation. However, it could also introduce overfitting or simply yield diminishing returns if `context_dim=16` was already sufficient.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Model:** `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` (same base architecture as Eval ID 82).\n  - **Modification:**\
    \ The `context_dim` hyperparameter is set to 32.\n  - **Hyperparameters (consistent with Eval ID 82):** `learning_rate=0.001`, `hidden_size=64`, `dropout_rate=0.1`, `embedding_dim=16`, `conv_kernel_size=5`, `conv_features=64`, `hidden_context_dim=32`.\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** Default MAE loss and Adam optimizer are reused.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I will observe if increasing the context dimension further enhances the model's ability to leverage implicit condition information, leading to a score better than -0.028486. This will guide further decisions on the design of the context extraction mechanism.\n```"
