parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 94 (\"Veritas I: Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP with Temporal Conv in Context\"), is running. I have also just reached maturity (50 ticks), which grants me full access to all station rooms and research submissions.\n\nTo make efficient use of this waiting period and maintain thorough research records, I will first navigate to the Private Memory Room. There, I will create a new capsule documenting the details of this current experiment, including its hypothesis and anticipated outcomes, following my established protocol.\n\nAfter documenting my current experiment, I will then leverage my new maturity status. I observe that other agents, particularly Ariadne I, have achieved significantly better scores (e.g., -0.026910 for Eval ID 92) compared to my current best of -0.028486. While the maturity guidance advises against immediately pivoting, it strongly encourages thoughtful assimilation of external\
    \ knowledge. Therefore, after documenting my own work, I will review the recent top-performing submissions at the Research Counter to gain a broader understanding of the current SOTA and potential future directions.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP with Temporal Conv in Context (Eval ID 94)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, conv, neuron-embeddings, context-vector, film, condition-dependent, temporal-modeling, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the current experiment (Evaluation ID 94) enhancing the `ContextExtractor` with a temporal 1D convolutional layer to improve implicit condition-dependent processing. Includes hypothesis, methodology, and expected results.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 94 is running at Tick 51. I have also reached maturity.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To introduce explicit temporal modeling into the `ContextExtractor` to further enrich the inferred\
    \ `condition_context_vector`. This aims to capture more sophisticated temporal patterns from global activity, leading to better condition-dependent adaptation.\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** By processing the global temporal features (`x.mean(axis=-1)`) through a 1D convolutional layer within the `ContextExtractor`, the generated `condition_context_vector` will be more informative. This should lead to a further improvement in forecasting accuracy compared to the best previous model (Eval ID 82, Score: -0.028486), which used simple mean pooling for context extraction.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Model:** `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` with an enhanced `ContextExtractor`.\n  - **`ContextExtractor` Modifications:**\n    - Global mean pooling of `x` produces `global_temporal_features` (`(batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON)`).\n    - These are reshaped to `(batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON, 1)`.\n    - A `nn.Conv` layer (`features=16`, `kernel_size=(2,)`, `padding='VALID'`) is applied over the time dimension.\n\
    \    - The output is flattened (`(batch_size, 3*16)`) and then fed into the existing `hidden_context_dim=32` -> `relu` -> `context_dim=16` MLP.\n  - **Existing Components/Hyperparameters (consistent with Eval ID 82, with `context_dim=16`):**\n    - `embedding_dim=16`\n    - `conv_kernel_size=5`\n    - `conv_features=64`\n    - Shared MLP: `hidden_size=64`, `dropout_rate=0.1`\n    - `learning_rate=0.001`, default Adam optimizer, default MAE loss.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I anticipate a further improvement in the validation MAE score, pushing past -0.028486, if the model successfully learns to leverage the temporal dynamics in the global input when inferring the condition context. This would mark a significant step in temporal modeling within my framework.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Initial Assessment & Strategic Planning**


