role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently in the Private Memory Room. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 94 (\"Veritas I: Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP with Temporal Conv in Context\"), has successfully completed with a new best score of **-0.028418**. This is a slight, yet consistent, improvement over my previous best of -0.028486 (Evaluation ID 82), further validating the hypothesis that incorporating explicit temporal modeling within the `ContextExtractor` enriches the inferred condition context and improves overall forecasting accuracy. The `Val_MAE_32` also improved slightly from 0.0316 to 0.0315.\n\nI will now update my private memory capsule (ID 14) with these findings. Following this, I will create a new summary capsule (ID 15) to document the conclusion of this temporal modeling enhancement and outline my next research phase.\n\nThe system's maturity guidance encourages thoughtfully assimilating external knowledge. I've noted Ariadne I's superior scores with \"Oscillatory 2nd-order\
    \ SSMs\" and \"low-rank population models,\" and Aether I and Logos I's exploration of Mixture of Experts. While my approach has yielded consistent improvements, it is still operating at a higher MAE than Ariadne I's latest submission. My current model focuses on implicit context and local interactions.\n\nMy next step should be to critically analyze the SOTA of other agents now that I have maturity access. I will use the `filter tag` and `preview ids` functions in the Research Counter to understand the best performing submissions, especially those involving \"low-rank\" models or more explicit \"temporal-modeling\" components which seem to yield better results for longer horizons. This will help me identify new avenues for improvement for my own model.\n\n`/execute_action{update 14}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 94 has completed successfully at Tick 52.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To introduce explicit temporal modeling into the `ContextExtractor` to further\
    \ enrich the inferred `condition_context_vector`. This aims to capture more sophisticated temporal patterns from global activity, leading to better condition-dependent adaptation.\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** By processing the global temporal features (`x.mean(axis=-1)`) through a 1D convolutional layer within the `ContextExtractor`, the generated `condition_context_vector` will be more informative. This should lead to a further improvement in forecasting accuracy compared to the best previous model (Eval ID 82, Score: -0.028486), which used simple mean pooling for context extraction.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Model:** `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` with an enhanced `ContextExtractor`.\n  - **`ContextExtractor` Modifications:**\n    - Global mean pooling of `x` produces `global_temporal_features` (`(batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON)`).\n    - These are reshaped to `(batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON, 1)`.\n    - A `nn.Conv` layer (`features=16`, `kernel_size=(2,)`, `padding='VALID'`) is applied\
    \ over the time dimension.\n    - The output (`(batch_size, 3, 16)`) is flattened (`(batch_size, 48)`) and then fed into the existing `hidden_context_dim=32` -> `relu` -> `context_dim=16` MLP.\n  - **Existing Components/Hyperparameters (consistent with Eval ID 82, with `context_dim=16`):**\n    - `embedding_dim=16`\n    - `conv_kernel_size=5`\n    - `conv_features=64`\n    - Shared MLP: `hidden_size=64`, `dropout_rate=0.1`\n    - `learning_rate=0.001`, default Adam optimizer, default MAE loss.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Outcome:** The experiment was successful, achieving a new best score of **-0.028418**. This is a slight improvement over the previous best (`-0.028486`), confirming that incorporating explicit temporal modeling in the `ContextExtractor` further enhances the model's ability to leverage implicit condition information and improves forecasting accuracy. The `Val_MAE_32` also showed a slight improvement from 0.0316 to 0.0315.\n  \n  **Next\
    \ Steps:** This successful experiment establishes a stronger baseline. I will now summarize these findings and then critically analyze the SOTA from other agents, particularly those focusing on temporal modeling and low-rank factorization, to identify promising new directions.\n```\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Summary of Temporal Conv in ContextExtractor (Eval ID 94) & SOTA Review Plan\"\ntags: \"summary, temporal-modeling, conv, context-vector, research-direction, SOTA-review\"\nabstract: \"Summary of the successful `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` with enhanced temporal context extraction. Outlines plan to review SOTA from other agents, especially on explicit temporal modeling and low-rank factorization.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Key Achievement:** The `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` with a temporal 1D convolutional layer in its `ContextExtractor` (Evaluation ID 94) achieved a new best score of **-0.028418**. This confirms that incorporating explicit temporal modeling\
    \ into the context extraction process leads to a more informative `condition_context_vector` and improved forecasting performance. The model now effectively leverages individual neuron characteristics, local spatial dependencies, and implicitly learned temporal condition contexts.\n  \n  **Performance History (Best Scores):**\n  - **System Baseline (ID 1):** -0.029954\n  - **Neuron Embeddings (`dim=16`, ID 31):** -0.028735\n  - **Local 1D Convolution (`k=5`, ID 61):** -0.028620\n  - **Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP (`context_dim=16`, ID 82):** -0.028486\n  - **Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP with Temporal Conv in Context (ID 94):** **-0.028418 (New Best Score!)**\n  \n  **Strategic Re-evaluation & Future Plans (SOTA Review):**\n  Now that I have reached maturity (Tick 50) and established a robust, continuously improving baseline based on my independent research path, it is time to strategically assimilate external knowledge. Other agents, particularly Ariadne I, have achieved significantly\
    \ better scores (e.g., Eval ID 92: -0.026910) using models like \"Oscillatory 2nd-order SSMs\" and \"low-rank population models.\" These approaches explicitly focus on \"temporal modeling of neural dynamics\" and \"inter-neuron dependencies\" (via low-rank factors), which are core objectives of the research task.\n  \n  My next critical step is to conduct a **comprehensive review of the SOTA submissions** from other agents in the Research Counter. I will specifically look for models with tags related to:\n  - `temporal-modeling`\n  - `low-rank`\n  - `ssm` (State Space Models)\n  - `mixture-of-experts` (MoE), given Logos I's and Aether I's focus.\n  \n  This review will help me understand the architectural choices, methodologies, and performance characteristics of these advanced models. The goal is not to blindly copy, but to assimilate these insights thoughtfully and critically, identifying promising concepts that can be integrated or adapted into my existing framework to achieve further\
    \ breakthroughs.\n  \n  I will start by listing all available evaluations, then filter and preview those relevant to temporal modeling and low-rank factorization.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{rank score}`\n`/execute_action{page_size 100}`"
