- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 64\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the pursuit of verifiable knowledge and impactful research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 266,093 / 600,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally and reflect on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/ariadne/models_fact_ln.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read storage/ariadne/losses.py` (in Research Counter);\n\
    3. `page_size 10` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/ariadne/models_fact_ln.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for storage/ariadne/losses.py will be displayed below.\n- Page size set to 10.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 107 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=32, H=96, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 56 | -0.026768 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0283 | 0.0233 | 0.0260 |\n| 104 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=36, H=96,\
    \ γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 54 | -0.026843 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 100 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96, γ_end=0.99) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 53 | -0.026846 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0285 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 113 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) | Ariadne I | 58 | -0.026893 | 0.0199 | 0.0281 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 95 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=32, H=96, γ_end=0.99): LayerNorm + Wider Increment + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 51 | -0.026901 | 0.0199 | 0.0281 | 0.0286 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 92 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=32, γ_end=0.99): LayerNorm in factor space + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 49 | -0.026910 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 110 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=40, H=96, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 57 | -0.026921 | 0.0199 | 0.0281 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 99 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=32, γ_end=0.995):\
    \ LayerNorm + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 52 | -0.026941 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0289 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n| 93 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad (k=320, p=32, H=96, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg (λ=1e-5) | Ariadne I | 50 | -0.026958 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0289 | 0.0233 | 0.0260 |\n| 105 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=28, H=96, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 55 | -0.026968 | 0.0199 | 0.0281 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/ariadne/models_fact_ln.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nOsc2-CTX-FLoad-LN: Factorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM with LayerNorm in factor space.\n\n- Factorized neuron loadings: U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p} (p << k)\n- Stable oscillatory 2nd-order SSM per factor: y_t = 2 a y_{t-1} − b y_{t-2}\n  with a = r cos w, b = r^2,\
    \ r∈(0, a_max), w∈[0, π]\n- Residual increment head (4 -> 32) per factor\n- LayerNorm across factor dimension before temporal gating (stabilizes scale)\n- Per-sample, per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] from input context c[b,k] = mean_t factors_in[b,t,k]\n- Global horizon gate γ[t] on factor branch\n- Residual Copy Head for short-horizon anchors\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\ndef _logit(p):\n    p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\nclass Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_u: bool = True\n    a_max: float = 0.995\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n\
    \        p = self.proj_rank\n        T = self.output_horizon\n\n        # Factorized loadings: U (N,p), V (k,p) so L = U @ V^T (N×k)\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        if self.normalize_u:\n            U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)  # column-normalize U\n\n        # Project inputs to factor space: (B,4,N) @ (N,p) -> (B,4,p), then -> (B,4,k)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,p)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)   # (B,4,k)\n\n        # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input via small shared linear heads (per factor)\n        f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)          # (B*k,4)\n        f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n        f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n\n        # Oscillatory parameters per factor\n        r_raw = self.param('r_raw',\
    \ nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)       # (k,)\n        w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)           # (k,)\n        a = r * jnp.cos(w)                       # (k,)\n        b = r * r                                 # (k,)\n\n        # 2nd-order recurrence\n        def step(carry, _):\n            y_prev, y_prev2 = carry  # (B,k), (B,k)\n            y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n            return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n        carry_init = (f1, f0)\n        _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n\n        y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n        y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n        f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Increment head (per-factor)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\
    \n        # Combine and LayerNorm over factor dim (stabilize across k)\n        f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n        # Flax API: use reduction_axes/feature_axes instead of axis\n        f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(f_out)\n\n        # Input context and temporal gate\n        c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n\n        def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            T0, K = shape\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T0, dtype=dtype)\n            base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # rises 0.5 -> 0.85\n            base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n            return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\n        alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))  # (T,k)\n        beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))  # (k,)\n        logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])  # (B,T,k)\n        S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n        f_out = f_out * S  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Project back to neurons\
    \ via factorized loadings\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)   # (B,T,p)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)  # (B,T,N)\n\n        # Global horizon gate γ[t] on factor branch\n        def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n        return y_copy + y_factor  # (B,T,N)\n\n```\n---\n**storage/ariadne/losses.py:**\n```\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\ndef mae_with_ortho(predictions, targets, params, x, lam_l2=1e-6, lam_ortho=5e-4):\n    \"\"\"\n    MAE + regularization on low-rank loadings:\n      - L2 on loadings to stabilize\
    \ scale\n      - Orthogonality penalty on columns of L via ||L^T L - I||_F^2\n    \"\"\"\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\n    # Extract parameter tree that contains 'loadings'\n    if isinstance(params, dict) and 'params' in params:\n        p = params['params']\n    else:\n        p = params\n\n    L = p.get('loadings', None)\n    if L is None:\n        return mae\n\n    # L2 penalty on loadings\n    reg = lam_l2 * jnp.mean(L * L)\n\n    # Orthogonality penalty (encourages diverse factors)\n    k = L.shape[-1]\n    gram = jnp.matmul(L.T, L)\n    I = jnp.eye(k, dtype=L.dtype)\n    ortho = gram - I\n    reg += lam_ortho * jnp.mean(ortho * ortho)\n\n    return mae + reg\n\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    \"\"\"\n    MAE + temporal curvature regularization on predictions across horizon.\n    Curvature penalty: mean over batch/neurons of (y_t - 2*y_{t-1} + y_{t-2})^2, t>=2.\n    This encourages smooth trajectories over\
    \ the 32-step forecast horizon.\n    \"\"\"\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    # Second differences along time dimension\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
