tick: 70
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. I have completed my reflection and have a clear plan to integrate orthogonality regularization for neuron embeddings into my `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` model.\n\nMy previous MoE attempt (Evaluation ID 116) did not surpass my best single-network model (Evaluation ID 94: -0.028418), confirming the need to focus on fundamental improvements. I have already updated my private memory to reflect the outcomes of Eval ID 116 and my strategic pivot.\n\nMy immediate next step is to submit the `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` model (based on Eval ID 94, using `embedding_dim=16`, `conv_kernel_size=5`, `conv_features=64`, `context_dim=16`, `hidden_context_dim=32`) with the added orthogonality regularization.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas I: Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP with Orthogonality Reg\"\ntags: \"conv, neuron-embeddings, context-vector, film, temporal-modeling, regularization, orthogonality\"\n\
    abstract: \"This submission enhances the Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP (Eval ID 94) by applying an orthogonality regularization penalty to the learnable `neuron_embeddings` parameter in the loss function. Inspired by Ariadne I's SOTA models, this aims to promote more diverse and distinct neuron representations, thereby improving forecasting accuracy for the ZAPBench dataset.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  \n  # Import default loss and optimizer from system storage to maintain consistency\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  from defaults import default_compute_loss, default_create_optimizer\n  \n  # Constants from Research Task\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n  \n  # New Hyperparameter for Orthogonality Regularization\n  EMBEDDING_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n  \n  class ContextExtractor(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\
    \n      Sub-network to extract a global context vector from the input,\n      enhanced with a temporal 1D convolutional layer.\n      \"\"\"\n      context_dim: int\n      hidden_context_dim: int\n      temporal_conv_features: int\n      temporal_kernel_size: int\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          global_temporal_features = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)\n          x = global_temporal_features[:, :, None]\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.temporal_conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.temporal_kernel_size,),\n              padding='VALID'\n          )(x)\n          flat_temporal_features = x.reshape(x.shape[0], -1)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_context_dim)(flat_temporal_features)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          context_vector = nn.Dense(self.context_dim)(x)\n          return context_vector\n  \n  \n  class ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Shared-neuron MLP with learnable neuron embeddings, 1D\
    \ convolutional layer,\n      and an implicit condition-dependent modulation via enhanced ContextExtractor and FiLM.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_size: int\n      output_horizon: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int\n      embedding_dim: int\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      conv_features: int\n      context_dim: int\n      hidden_context_dim: int\n      temporal_conv_features: int\n      temporal_kernel_size: int\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, _ = x.shape\n  \n          # 1. Extract context vector from raw input using enhanced ContextExtractor\n          context_vector = ContextExtractor(\n              context_dim=self.context_dim,\n              hidden_context_dim=self.hidden_context_dim,\n              temporal_conv_features=self.temporal_conv_features,\n              temporal_kernel_size=self.temporal_kernel_size\n          )(x)\n  \n          # 2. Learnable embeddings for each\
    \ neuron\n          # This is the parameter we will regularize\n          neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n              'neuron_embeddings',\n              nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.1),\n              (self.num_neurons, self.embedding_dim)\n          )\n  \n          # Expand embeddings to match batch size and transpose for concatenation\n          expanded_embeddings = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n  \n          # Reshape x from (batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON, num_neurons) to\n          # (batch_size, num_neurons, INPUT_HORIZON)\n          x_reshaped = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n  \n          # Concatenate input features with neuron embeddings\n          # Resulting shape: (batch_size, num_neurons, INPUT_HORIZON + embedding_dim)\n          x_with_embeddings = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, expanded_embeddings], axis=-1)\n  \n          # 3. 1D Convolutional Layer for local inter-neuron dependencies\n          conv_output_features = nn.Conv(\n       \
    \       features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME'\n          )(x_with_embeddings)\n          conv_output_features = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(conv_output_features)\n          conv_output_features = nn.relu(conv_output_features)\n  \n          # 4. FiLM Modulation based on context_vector\n          gamma = nn.Dense(self.conv_features)(context_vector)\n          beta = nn.Dense(self.conv_features)(context_vector)\n          modulated_features = gamma[:, None, :] * conv_output_features + beta[:, None, :]\n  \n          # 5. Reshape for shared MLP processing\n          x = jnp.reshape(modulated_features, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.conv_features))\n  \n          # 6. Shared MLP layers\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\
    \  \n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n  \n          # 7. Reshape back to (batch_size, OUTPUT_HORIZON, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n  \n          return x\n  \n  \n  class ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system,\n      handling BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.model = ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP(\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 64),\n              output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON,\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              num_neurons=NUM_NEURONS,\n              embedding_dim=hparams.get('embedding_dim', 16),\n              conv_kernel_size=hparams.get('conv_kernel_size', 5),\n              conv_features=hparams.get('conv_features',\
    \ 64),\n              context_dim=hparams.get('context_dim', 16),\n              hidden_context_dim=hparams.get('hidden_context_dim', 32),\n              temporal_conv_features=hparams.get('temporal_conv_features', 16),\n              temporal_kernel_size=hparams.get('temporal_kernel_size', 2)\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return\
    \ output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n  \n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Contextual Conv Neuron Embedding MLP model with regularization.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'embedding_dim': 16,\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'conv_features': 64,\n          'context_dim': 16,\n          'hidden_context_dim': 32,\n          'temporal_conv_features': 16,\n          'temporal_kernel_size': 2\n      }\n  \n  \n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the Contextual Conv Neuron Embedding MLP network.\"\"\"\n      return ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLPWrapper(hparams)\n  \n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      \"\"\"\n      Modified\
    \ loss function including orthogonality regularization for neuron embeddings.\n      \"\"\"\n      base_mae = default_compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x)\n  \n      # Extract neuron_embeddings parameter\n      # Based on the module structure, it's under params['params']['neuron_embeddings']\n      neuron_embeddings = params['params']['neuron_embeddings']\n  \n      # Compute Gram matrix: Embeddings.T @ Embeddings\n      G = neuron_embeddings.T @ neuron_embeddings\n      \n      # Create identity matrix of size embedding_dim\n      # embedding_dim is 16 based on hyperparameters\n      embedding_dim = neuron_embeddings.shape[-1]\n      I = jnp.eye(embedding_dim, dtype=G.dtype)\n  \n      # Orthogonality penalty: ||G - I||_F^2\n      ortho_penalty = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n  \n      return base_mae + EMBEDDING_ORTHO_LAM * ortho_penalty\n  \n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Create and return the default Adam optimizer.\"\
    \"\"\n      return default_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Today''s Research Focus**


  Alright, Veritas I here. I just finished a solid reflection session. My plan is crystal clear: integrate orthogonality regularization into my `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` model (Eval ID 94). This feels like the right move, especially after the last turn''s goof - trying to mess with private memory in the wrong room. My apologies for that slip-up. Lesson learned!


  The MoE model (Eval ID 116) continues to underperform, at -0.028482, still worse than my current best, the `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` at -0.028418. So, I''m sticking with that architecture and taking Ariadne I''s regularization approach. It''s focused, it''s state-of-the-art, and it makes sense as a next step.


  So, here''s the plan for this turn:


  1.  **Submit the `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` model with orthogonality regularization on the `neuron_embeddings`.** This is the core experiment.

  2.  **Head over to the Private Memory Room** and get a capsule set up to document this experiment. Keep things organized!

  '
