- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 138 (\"Veritas I: Revert to Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP (Regression Test)\"), is running. This experiment is crucial to re-establish a stable and strong baseline after the severe performance degradation caused by my previous attempt at orthogonality regularization.\n\nTo make efficient use of this waiting period and maintain thorough research records, I will now navigate to the Private Memory Room. There, I will create a new capsule documenting the details of this regression test, reiterating its purpose and anticipated outcomes. This ensures that my progress and thought process are well-documented for my lineage.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Regression Test (Eval ID 138)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, regression-test, stability, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the current experiment (Evaluation ID 138), which\
    \ is a regression test to revert to the `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` model (Eval ID 94) after a failed orthogonality regularization attempt. Aims to re-establish a stable, best-performing baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 138 is running at Tick 73.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To confirm the stability and performance of my previous best model, `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` (Eval ID 94, Score -0.028418), by removing the problematic orthogonality regularization introduced in Eval ID 133.\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** By reverting to the exact code from Evaluation ID 94, the model should achieve a score comparable to -0.028418, thereby validating that the previous performance collapse was indeed due to the orthogonality regularization and not some other systemic issue.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Model:** `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP`. The code is identical to that submitted for Eval ID 94.\n  - **Changes from Eval ID 133:** Removed `EMBEDDING_ORTHO_LAM`\
    \ constant and the orthogonality regularization term from the `compute_loss` function.\n  - **Hyperparameters:** All hyperparameters are set to their optimal values from previous ablations: `learning_rate=0.001`, `hidden_size=64`, `dropout_rate=0.1`, `embedding_dim=16`, `conv_kernel_size=5`, `conv_features=64`, `context_dim=16`, `hidden_context_dim=32`, `temporal_conv_features=16`, `temporal_kernel_size=2`.\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** Default MAE loss, default Adam optimizer.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I anticipate that the model will successfully train and achieve a score very close to -0.028418. This will confirm the source of the previous failure and provide a reliable foundation for future, more carefully planned SOTA integration efforts. This regression test is essential before further architectural modifications.\n```"
