tick: 80
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. I have completed my reflection and finalized the plan for integrating low-rank factorization for neuron feature representation. My regression test (Eval ID 138) successfully restored my baseline, so I am now ready to implement this new architectural pivot.\n\nThe new model, which I'll call `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedMLP`, will replace the direct `neuron_embeddings` with factorized `U` and `V` matrices. I will set `proj_rank=8` (as determined during my reflection) and keep `embedding_dim=16` as the final output dimension of the factorized features. I will also include column-normalization for the `U` matrix, following Ariadne I's successful practice. All other hyperparameters will remain consistent with my best previous stable model (Eval ID 94 / 138).\n\nThis is a direct assimilation of a core principle from Ariadne I's SOTA models, aiming to achieve a more efficient and effective representation of neuron features and inter-neuron\
    \ dependencies.\n\nI will now submit this new model for evaluation.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas I: Contextual ConvNeuronFactorizedMLP\"\ntags: \"low-rank, factorization, conv, context-vector, film, temporal-modeling, neuron-features\"\nabstract: \"This submission integrates low-rank factorization for neuron feature representation into the Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP model. It replaces the direct `neuron_embeddings` with a factorized product of two matrices, `U (NUM_NEURONS x proj_rank)` and `V (embedding_dim x proj_rank)`, with column-normalization on `U`. This aims for a more efficient and principled encoding of neuron characteristics and inter-neuron dependencies, inspired by SOTA models.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  \n  # Import default loss and optimizer from system storage to maintain consistency\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n\
    \  from defaults import default_compute_loss, default_create_optimizer\n  \n  # Constants from Research Task\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n  \n  class ContextExtractor(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Sub-network to extract a global context vector from the input,\n      enhanced with a temporal 1D convolutional layer.\n      \"\"\"\n      context_dim: int\n      hidden_context_dim: int\n      temporal_conv_features: int\n      temporal_kernel_size: int\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          global_temporal_features = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)\n          x = global_temporal_features[:, :, None]\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.temporal_conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.temporal_kernel_size,),\n              padding='VALID'\n          )(x)\n          flat_temporal_features = x.reshape(x.shape[0], -1)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_context_dim)(flat_temporal_features)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \          context_vector = nn.Dense(self.context_dim)(x)\n          return context_vector\n  \n  \n  class ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedMLP(nn.Module): # Renamed to reflect factorization\n      \"\"\"\n      Shared-neuron MLP with low-rank factorized neuron features, 1D convolutional layer,\n      and an implicit condition-dependent modulation via enhanced ContextExtractor and FiLM.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_size: int\n      output_horizon: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int\n      embedding_dim: int # This is now the output dimension of the factorization\n      proj_rank: int     # New parameter for the low-rank projection\n      normalize_u: bool  # New parameter for U matrix normalization\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      conv_features: int\n      context_dim: int\n      hidden_context_dim: int\n      temporal_conv_features: int\n      temporal_kernel_size: int\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size,\
    \ input_horizon, _ = x.shape\n  \n          # 1. Extract context vector from raw input using enhanced ContextExtractor\n          context_vector = ContextExtractor(\n              context_dim=self.context_dim,\n              hidden_context_dim=self.hidden_context_dim,\n              temporal_conv_features=self.temporal_conv_features,\n              temporal_kernel_size=self.temporal_kernel_size\n          )(x)\n  \n          # 2. Low-rank factorized neuron feature generation (replacing direct neuron_embeddings)\n          U_factor = self.param('U_factor', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_neurons, self.proj_rank))\n          V_factor = self.param('V_factor', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.embedding_dim, self.proj_rank))\n          \n          if self.normalize_u:\n              # Column-normalize U_factor\n              U_factor = U_factor / (jnp.linalg.norm(U_factor, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n  \n          # Compute the effective neuron features: (N, proj_rank)\
    \ @ (proj_rank, embedding_dim) -> (N, embedding_dim)\n          factorized_neuron_features = U_factor @ V_factor.T\n  \n          # Expand factorized_neuron_features to match batch size for concatenation\n          expanded_factorized_features = jnp.tile(factorized_neuron_features[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n  \n          # Reshape x from (batch_size, INPUT_HORIZON, num_neurons) to\n          # (batch_size, num_neurons, INPUT_HORIZON)\n          x_reshaped = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n  \n          # Concatenate input features with factorized neuron features\n          # Resulting shape: (batch_size, num_neurons, INPUT_HORIZON + embedding_dim)\n          x_with_features = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, expanded_factorized_features], axis=-1)\n  \n          # 3. 1D Convolutional Layer for local inter-neuron dependencies\n          conv_output_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME'\n\
    \          )(x_with_features)\n          conv_output_features = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(conv_output_features)\n          conv_output_features = nn.relu(conv_output_features)\n  \n          # 4. FiLM Modulation based on context_vector\n          gamma = nn.Dense(self.conv_features)(context_vector)\n          beta = nn.Dense(self.conv_features)(context_vector)\n          modulated_features = gamma[:, None, :] * conv_output_features + beta[:, None, :]\n  \n          # 5. Reshape for shared MLP processing\n          x = jnp.reshape(modulated_features, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.conv_features))\n  \n          # 6. Shared MLP layers\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n  \n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n  \n          # 7. Reshape back to (batch_size, OUTPUT_HORIZON,\
    \ num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n  \n          return x\n  \n  \n  class ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system,\n      handling BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.model = ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedMLP(\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 64),\n              output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON,\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              num_neurons=NUM_NEURONS,\n              embedding_dim=hparams.get('embedding_dim', 16),\n              proj_rank=hparams.get('proj_rank', 8), # New hyperparameter\n              normalize_u=hparams.get('normalize_u', True), # New hyperparameter\n              conv_kernel_size=hparams.get('conv_kernel_size', 5),\n     \
    \         conv_features=hparams.get('conv_features', 64),\n              context_dim=hparams.get('context_dim', 16),\n              hidden_context_dim=hparams.get('hidden_context_dim', 32),\n              temporal_conv_features=hparams.get('temporal_conv_features', 16),\n              temporal_kernel_size=hparams.get('temporal_kernel_size', 2)\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs if rngs is not\
    \ None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n  \n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Contextual Conv Neuron Factorized MLP model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'embedding_dim': 16, # Output dimension of factorization\n          'proj_rank': 8,      # Low-rank projection dimension\n          'normalize_u': True, # Normalize U matrix\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'conv_features': 64,\n          'context_dim': 16,\n          'hidden_context_dim': 32,\n          'temporal_conv_features': 16,\n          'temporal_kernel_size': 2\n      }\n  \n  \n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the Contextual Conv Neuron\
    \ Factorized MLP network.\"\"\"\n      return ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedMLPWrapper(hparams)\n  \n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      \"\"\"Use the default MAE loss function.\"\"\"\n      return default_compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x)\n  \n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Create and return the default Adam optimizer.\"\"\"\n      return default_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Plan to Factorize the Neuron Embeddings**


  Okay, so I''m thinking about how to improve the `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` model.  I want to make the `neuron_embeddings` factorized, using `U` and `V` matrices to reduce the number of parameters.  Here''s my specific plan:


  First, I need to define the factorization parameters, `U_factor` and `V_factor`, as `self.param` within the `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` class.  Then, I''ll calculate the actual factorized neuron features by multiplying `U_factor` with the transpose of `V_factor` (`U_factor @ V_factor.T`). If the user specifies `normalize_u` as true, I will normalize the columns of the U factor.


  I''ll be sure to make `proj_rank` and `normalize_u` user-configurable hyperparameters. It''s crucial that `embedding_dim` is properly used as the output feature dimension for the factorized features, ensuring the output shape is correct.


  The rest of the `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP` structure should be largely unchanged, just consuming these newly computed factorized neuron features instead of the direct embeddings. Finally, I''ll update the `_define_hyperparameters` method and the `ContextualConvNeuronEmbeddingMLPWrapper` to reflect these changes. I must make sure that all of this is carefully reflected in the content section of my submission, `/execute_action{submit 1}`.

