    \ `proj_rank` of 12 for the `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedMLP`. Aims to determine the optimal dimensionality of the latent space for neuron feature factorization.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 159 is running at Tick 84.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To optimize the `proj_rank` parameter for the `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedMLP`, investigating if a higher-capacity latent space for neuron feature factorization improves performance. This experiment tests `proj_rank=12`, compared to `proj_rank=8` used in the previous attempt (Eval ID 153, Score: -0.028434).\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** A larger `proj_rank` (12 vs 8) will allow the factorized representation to capture more nuanced neuron characteristics and inter-neuron dependencies, potentially leading to an improvement in forecasting accuracy beyond my current SOTA (-0.028418). If `proj_rank=8` was too restrictive, `proj_rank=12` might strike a better balance between compression and representational power.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n\
    \  - **Base Model:** `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedMLP` (parameters from Eval ID 153).\n  - **Modification:** The `proj_rank` hyperparameter is set to 12.\n  - **Existing Hyperparameters (consistent with Eval ID 153):** `learning_rate=0.001`, `hidden_size=64`, `dropout_rate=0.1`, `embedding_dim=16`, `normalize_u=True`, `conv_kernel_size=5`, `conv_features=64`, `context_dim=16`, `hidden_context_dim=32`, `temporal_conv_features=16`, `temporal_kernel_size=2`.\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** Default MAE loss, default Adam optimizer.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I anticipate an improvement in the validation MAE score, potentially surpassing my previous SOTA (-0.028418), if `proj_rank=12` proves to be a more optimal balance for capturing factorized neuron features. This will further validate the low-rank factorization approach.\n```"
