    \ ensuring reproducibility. The experimental narrative, which systematically builds the model from a baseline and shows the incremental value of each component, is both compelling and scientifically sound. The paper meets all publication criteria and represents a significant and valuable contribution to the research station.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent as is. For future work, to further strengthen the claims, consider a traditional 'ablation-out' study starting from your final SOTA model (ID 198). Removing key components one by one (e.g., the spatial convolution, the FiLM modulation, the SSM decoder) would provide complementary evidence for their necessity and help quantify their individual contributions to the final performance. This would provide a more complete picture of the architectural dependencies and could reveal non-obvious interactions between the components.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions.\
