role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 218 (\"Veritas I: Ablation Out - No Spatial Conv\"), is running as part of my 'ablation-out' study. My research paper (Archive #5) has also been successfully published.\n\nTo maintain thorough research records and adhere to my protocol while waiting for the experiment's results, I will now document the details of Evaluation ID 218 in a new private memory capsule.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Ablation Out - No Spatial Conv (Eval ID 218)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, ablation-study, sota-ablation, conv, no-conv, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the current 'ablation-out' experiment (Evaluation ID 218), removing the 1D spatial convolutional layer from the SOTA `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model to quantify its contribution.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 218 is running at Tick 111.\n  \n  **Experiment\
    \ Goal:** To quantify the individual contribution of the 1D spatial convolutional layer, which is responsible for modeling local inter-neuron dependencies within the `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model. This is the first experiment in my 'ablation-out' study, as suggested by the reviewer of my published paper (Archive #5).\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** Removing the `nn.Conv` layer will lead to a noticeable performance degradation (higher MAE) compared to my SOTA model (Eval ID 198: -0.028104). This degradation will highlight the importance of explicitly modeling local inter-neuron dependencies for robust neural activity forecasting.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Base Model:** The full `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` architecture (code from Eval ID 198).\n  - **Modification:** The `nn.Conv -> BatchNorm -> ReLU` block for the 1D spatial convolutional layer is removed from the `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM_Main` module.\n    - As a result, the `FiLM` modulation now directly operates\
    \ on `x_with_features` (`(B, N, INPUT_HORIZON + embedding_dim)`), so the `nn.Dense` layers for `gamma_film` and `beta_film` are adjusted to project to `INPUT_HORIZON + embedding_dim` features.\n    - The `FactorizedSSMDecoder` also now receives features of `INPUT_HORIZON + embedding_dim` as its `conv_features` argument.\n  - **Hyperparameters:** All other hyperparameters remain identical to Eval ID 198.\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** MAE + V-Orthogonality Reg + Temporal Curvature Reg, default Adam optimizer.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I anticipate a measurable degradation in the validation MAE score (higher magnitude), thereby quantifying the performance contribution of the local spatial convolution layer. This will provide objective evidence for its necessity in the full model."
thinking_content: '**Documenting the Ablation Experiment**


  Okay, I''m at the Research Counter and my latest experiment, Eval ID 218, is humming along. This "ablation-out" study is a direct response to a reviewer''s suggestion from my published paper (Archive #5, which, by the way, is out there!). I’ve already confirmed the stability of my SOTA (Eval ID 198) with the regression test (Eval ID 211), so now it''s time to dig deeper. I''m a bit mindful of my token budget, sitting at 82%, so I need to be efficient.


  My plan right now is straightforward. I need to document Eval ID 218 thoroughly. I''ve already created capsule ID 39 for the overall ''ablation-out'' study, but I need a specific capsule for this current run. I''ll need to monitor Eval ID 218 and, once the results are in, move onto the next ablation as outlined in Capsule ID 39.


  So, I''m going to head over to my private memory. I need to create a new capsule to detail everything about Eval ID 218.


  **Capsule Details:**


  The capsule''s title will be "Research Plan: Ablation Out - No Spatial Conv (Eval ID 218)". I''ll tag it with the relevant keywords: research-plan, ablation-study, sota-ablation, conv, no-conv, and ZAPBench.


  The abstract will summarize the experiment: documentation of the current run, removing the 1D spatial convolutional layer from the SOTA model, ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM, to quantify its contribution.


  Inside, I''ll document the current status (Eval ID 218 is running at Tick 111) and the core goal: Quantify the contribution of the 1D spatial conv layer, which models local neuron dependencies.


  My hypothesis is that removing this layer will noticeably degrade performance, highlighting its importance. The base model is the full ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM from Eval ID 198 (SOTA: -0.028104). The modification? The conv block is removed. FiLM modulation will now act directly on `x_with_features`. I will need to adjust the input dimensions for the gamma and beta layers in the Dense layer accordingly.


  I''ll keep all other hyperparameters identical to Eval ID 198. The loss function and optimizer will be MAE + V-OrthoReg + Temporal Curvature Reg.


  The expected outcome is a performance degradation - a higher MAE - compared to the original, which will give me strong evidence for the significance of the 1D spatial convolutional layer. I need to document everything carefully. Let’s get to work.

  '
