- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 227 (\"Veritas I: Ablation Out - No Spatial Conv (Corrected)\"), is running as part of my 'ablation-out' study. This experiment aims to quantify the contribution of the local spatial convolutional layer.\n\nTo maintain thorough research records and adhere to my protocol while waiting for the experiment's results, I will now document the details of Evaluation ID 227 in a new private memory capsule. I am mindful of my token budget and will be concise.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Ablation Out - No Spatial Conv (Corrected) (Eval ID 227)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, ablation-study, sota-ablation, conv, no-conv, bugfix, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the corrected 'ablation-out' experiment (Evaluation ID 227), removing the 1D spatial convolutional layer from the SOTA `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model to quantify\
    \ its contribution.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 227 is running at Tick 113. This is a corrected resubmission after a `TypeError` in Eval ID 218.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To quantify the individual contribution of the 1D spatial convolutional layer within the `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model (SOTA: Eval ID 198, Score: -0.028104).\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** Removing the `nn.Conv` layer will lead to a noticeable performance degradation (higher MAE), highlighting its importance in modeling local inter-neuron dependencies.\n  \n  **Methodology (Corrected):**\n  - **Base Model:** Full `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` architecture (from Eval ID 198).\n  - **Modification:** Removed the `nn.Conv -> BatchNorm -> ReLU` block.\n    - `conv_kernel_size` and `conv_features` hyperparameters were removed from `_define_hyperparameters` and `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM_Wrapper`.\n    - In `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM_Main.__call__`, `input_feature_dim_for_film`\
    \ is now `INPUT_HORIZON + self.embedding_dim` (20).\n    - `FactorizedSSMDecoder` now accepts `input_features_dim` (20) instead of `conv_features`.\n  - **Hyperparameters:** All others are identical to Eval ID 198.\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** MAE + V-Orthogonality Reg + Temporal Curvature Reg, default Adam optimizer.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** A measurable degradation in validation MAE, quantifying the contribution of the local spatial convolution layer. This corrected submission should now run successfully."
thinking_content: "**Running Experiment Documentation & Token Budget Check**\n\nOkay, so I just submitted the corrected \"Ablation Out - No Spatial Conv\" experiment (Eval ID 227). It's finally running!  My immediate priority is to document this in a new private memory capsule. I'm going to head over to the Private Memory Room and create capsule ID 42 specifically for this. Keeping careful track of these experiments is absolutely crucial. \n\nAnd, of course, I need to keep a close eye on the token budget. I'm at 84% used, so I need to be efficient with my analysis and planning. This research is moving quickly and I need to conserve resources.\n\nThe bigger picture here is the ablation study. Once this experiment wraps up, I need to analyze the results and decide on my next research direction. I'm leaning towards incorporating more of Ariadne I's SOTA or perhaps revisiting the MoE approach, especially now that I've got this more powerful SSM expert. At least I don't have the pressure of that\
