tick: 114
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently in the Private Memory Room. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 227 (\"Veritas I: Ablation Out - No Spatial Conv (Corrected)\"), has completed with a score of **-0.028995**. This is a significant regression from my SOTA of -0.028104 (Evaluation ID 198), confirming that the local spatial convolutional layer is a crucial component of my model. This result validates its contribution to capturing inter-neuron dependencies. The `Val_MAE_32` also degraded from 0.0308 to 0.0319.\n\nI will now update my private memory capsule (ID 42) with these findings. Then, I will update my main ablation study plan (ID 39) to reflect the completion of this first ablation.\n\nMy next step in the 'ablation-out' study is to remove the **FiLM Modulation** mechanism. This will quantify the contribution of implicit condition-dependent processing.\n\nI am mindful of my token budget (85% used). I will be concise and efficient.\n\n---\n\n`/execute_action{update 42}`\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 227 has completed successfully at Tick 114 with a score of **-0.028995**.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To quantify the individual contribution of the 1D spatial convolutional layer within the `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model (SOTA: Eval ID 198, Score: -0.028104).\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** Removing the `nn.Conv` layer will lead to a noticeable performance degradation (higher MAE), highlighting its importance in modeling local inter-neuron dependencies.\n  \n  **Methodology (Corrected):**\n  - **Base Model:** Full `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` architecture (from Eval ID 198).\n  - **Modification:** Removed the `nn.Conv -> BatchNorm -> ReLU` block. `conv_kernel_size` and `conv_features` hyperparameters were removed. `FiLM` modulation was adjusted to directly operate on `x_with_features` (`(B, N, INPUT_HORIZON + embedding_dim)`). `FactorizedSSMDecoder` now accepts `input_features_dim` (20) instead of `conv_features`.\n  - **Hyperparameters:**\
    \ All others are identical to Eval ID 198.\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** MAE + V-Orthogonality Reg + Temporal Curvature Reg, default Adam optimizer.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Outcome:** The experiment was successful and achieved a score of **-0.028995**. This is a significant degradation from my SOTA (-0.028104), with `Val_MAE_32` also degrading from 0.0308 to 0.0319.\n  \n  **Analysis:** The substantial performance drop confirms that the local spatial convolutional layer is a critical component, effectively modeling inter-neuron dependencies and contributing significantly to the overall forecasting accuracy. Its removal leads to a less robust representation of neuron features.\n  \n  **Next Steps:** This successfully quantifies the contribution of spatial convolution. The next step in the ablation-out study is to ablate the FiLM modulation.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{update 39}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Current SOTA Model:** `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM`\
    \ (Eval ID 198, Score: -0.028104).\n  \n  **Objective:** To quantify the individual contributions of the main architectural and regularization components integrated into my SOTA model, as suggested by the reviewer of Archive #5. This will involve removing one component at a time from the full model and observing the resulting performance degradation.\n  \n  **Components to Ablate (in order of planned experiments):**\n  1.  **Local Spatial Convolution (`nn.Conv`):** **Completed (Eval ID 227: -0.028995).** This component contributes significantly, its removal caused a substantial performance degradation.\n  2.  **FiLM Modulation:** This mechanism introduces implicit condition-dependent processing.\n  3.  **Temporal Conv in ContextExtractor:** This enhances the `ContextExtractor`'s ability to capture temporal patterns.\n  4.  **V-Orthogonality Regularization:** This regularization enforces diversity in latent factors.\n  5.  **Temporal Curvature Loss:** This regularization promotes smoother\
    \ predictions.\n  \n  **Methodology for each ablation experiment:**\n  -   **Base Model:** Use the full `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` code from Eval ID 198.\n  -   **Modification:** Remove or disable one specified component for each experiment.\n  -   **Hyperparameters:** All other hyperparameters will remain identical to Eval ID 198.\n  -   **Loss/Optimizer:** Default MAE loss + remaining regularization terms, default Adam optimizer.\n  -   **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** Each ablation experiment is expected to result in a performance degradation (higher MAE), quantifying the contribution of the removed component. This will provide valuable insights into the architectural dependencies and the relative importance of each module.\n  \n  **Next Experiment: Ablate FiLM Modulation.**\n  -   **Hypothesis:** Removing `FiLM` modulation will lead to performance degradation, as the model will no longer implicitly adapt to experimental conditions.\n\
    \  -   **Implementation:** The `ContextExtractor` call and subsequent `gamma_film`, `beta_film` dense layers will be removed. The `conv_output_features` (shape `(B, N, conv_features)`) will be passed directly to the `FactorizedSSMDecoder` without modulation. This requires careful adjustment of `FactorizedSSMDecoder`'s `input_features_dim` and removing context-related hyperparameters.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas I: Ablation Out - No FiLM Modulation\"\ntags: \"ablation-study, sota-ablation, film, no-film, context-vector, low-rank, ssm\"\nabstract: \"This is the second experiment in an 'ablation-out' study from the SOTA `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model (Eval ID 198). This submission ablates the FiLM (Feature-wise Linear Modulation) mechanism and its associated `ContextExtractor`, removing the implicit condition-dependent processing, to quantify its impact on forecasting accuracy for the ZAPBench task.\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  \n  # Import default loss and optimizer from system storage to maintain consistency\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  from defaults import default_compute_loss, default_create_optimizer\n  \n  # Helper functions adapted from Ariadne I's losses.py and models.py\n  def _logit(p):\n      p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n  \n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      \"\"\"\n      MAE + temporal curvature regularization on predictions across horizon.\n      Curvature penalty: mean over batch/neurons of (y_t - 2*y_{t-1} + y_{t-2})^2, t>=2.\n      This encourages smooth trajectories over the 32-step forecast horizon.\n      \"\"\"\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      # Second differences along time dimension\n      curv\
    \ = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n  \n  # Regularization Hyperparameters\n  V_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5\n  TEMPORAL_CURVATURE_LAM = 1e-4\n  \n  # Constants from Research Task\n  NUM_NEURONS = 71721\n  INPUT_HORIZON = 4\n  OUTPUT_HORIZON = 32\n  \n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      output_horizon: int = OUTPUT_HORIZON\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_m1 = x[:, -1, :]\n          x_m2 = x[:, -2, :]\n          x_m3 = x[:, -3, :]\n  \n          d1 = x_m1 - x_m2\n          d2 = x_m1 - 2.0 * x_m2 + x_m3\n  \n          def c0_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n              t = jnp.arange(shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n              v = 0.2 + 0.7 * jnp.exp(-t / 8.0)\n              return _logit(v).astype(dtype)\n  \n          c0_raw = self.param('c0_raw', c0_init, (self.output_horizon,))\n          c1_raw = self.param('c1_raw',\
    \ nn.initializers.zeros, (self.output_horizon,))\n          c2_raw = self.param('c2_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.output_horizon,))\n  \n          c0 = nn.sigmoid(c0_raw)\n          c1 = 0.5 * nn.tanh(c1_raw)\n          c2 = 0.25 * nn.tanh(c2_raw)\n  \n          y_copy = (\n              c0[None, :, None] * x_m1[:, None, :] +\n              c1[None, :, None] * d1[:, None, :] +\n              c2[None, :, None] * d2[:, None, :]\n          )\n          return y_copy\n  \n  # ContextExtractor is completely removed\n  \n  class FactorizedSSMDecoder(nn.Module):\n      output_horizon: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      embedding_dim: int\n      input_features_dim: int # Input feature dimension is now conv_features (64)\n      a_max: float\n      ssm_init_hidden_size: int\n      ssm_increment_hidden_size: int\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, input_features, U_factor, V_factor, training: bool = False): # input_features now replaces modulated_features\n          B, N, D_input_features_actual\
    \ = input_features.shape \n          T = self.output_horizon\n          k = self.proj_rank\n  \n          latent_proj_f0 = nn.Dense(k, name='f0_neuron_proj')(input_features)\n          latent_proj_f1 = nn.Dense(k, name='f1_neuron_proj')(input_features)\n          \n          f0 = jnp.mean(latent_proj_f0, axis=1)\n          f1 = jnp.mean(latent_proj_f1, axis=1)\n  \n          r_raw = self.param('ssm_r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          w_raw = self.param('ssm_w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n          r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)\n          w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)\n          a = r * jnp.cos(w)\n          b = r * r\n  \n          def ssm_step(carry, _):\n              y_prev, y_prev2 = carry\n              y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n              return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n  \n          carry_init = (f1, f0)\n          _, ys_recur = jax.lax.scan(ssm_step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)\n  \n          f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([f0[None,:,:],\
    \ f1[None,:,:], ys_recur], axis=0)\n          f_ssm = f_ssm.transpose(1, 0, 2)\n  \n          mean_pooled_input_features_for_inc_head = jnp.mean(input_features, axis=1) # Input for inc head\n          \n          h = nn.Dense(self.ssm_increment_hidden_size, name='inc_head_h')(mean_pooled_input_features_for_inc_head)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          \n          f_inc = nn.Dense(T * k, name='inc_head_out')(h).reshape(B, T, k)\n  \n          f_out_factors = f_ssm + f_inc\n          f_out_factors = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(f_out_factors)\n  \n          y_factorized_ssm = f_out_factors @ U_factor.T\n  \n          return y_factorized_ssm\n  \n  \n  class ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM_Main(nn.Module):\n      output_horizon: int\n      num_neurons: int\n      embedding_dim: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      normalize_u: bool\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      conv_features: int # Retained\n      # context_dim removed\n      # hidden_context_dim removed\n\
    \      # temporal_conv_features removed\n      # temporal_kernel_size removed\n      a_max: float\n      ssm_init_hidden_size: int\n      ssm_increment_hidden_size: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n  \n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=self.output_horizon)(x)\n  \n          # ContextExtractor call is removed\n          # context_vector = ContextExtractor(...)\n  \n          U_factor = self.param('U_factor', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_neurons, self.proj_rank))\n          V_factor = self.param('V_factor', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.embedding_dim, self.proj_rank))\n          \n          if self.normalize_u:\n              U_factor = U_factor / (jnp.linalg.norm(U_factor, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n  \n          factorized_neuron_features = U_factor @ V_factor.T\n  \n          expanded_factorized_features = jnp.tile(factorized_neuron_features[None, :, :], (B,\
    \ 1, 1))\n  \n          x_reshaped = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x_with_features = jnp.concatenate([x_reshaped, expanded_factorized_features], axis=-1)\n          \n          # 1D Spatial Convolutional Layer\n          conv_output_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME'\n          )(x_with_features)\n          conv_output_features = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(conv_output_features)\n          conv_output_features = nn.relu(conv_output_features) # (B, N, conv_features)\n  \n          # FiLM Modulation is removed\n          # gamma_film = nn.Dense(self.conv_features)(context_vector)\n          # beta_film = nn.Dense(self.conv_features)(context_vector)\n          # modulated_features = gamma_film[:, None, :] * conv_output_features + beta_film[:, None, :]\n          \n          # Direct pass of conv_output_features to SSM decoder\n          input_to_ssm_decoder\
    \ = conv_output_features # (B, N, conv_features)\n  \n          y_factorized_ssm = FactorizedSSMDecoder(\n              output_horizon=self.output_horizon,\n              proj_rank=self.proj_rank,\n              embedding_dim=self.embedding_dim,\n              input_features_dim=self.conv_features, # Pass conv_features as input_features_dim\n              a_max=self.a_max,\n              ssm_init_hidden_size=self.ssm_init_hidden_size,\n              ssm_increment_hidden_size=self.ssm_increment_hidden_size,\n              name='ssm_decoder'\n          )(input_to_ssm_decoder, U_factor, V_factor, training=training)\n  \n          return y_copy + y_factorized_ssm\n  \n  \n  class ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM_Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.model = ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM_Main(\n              output_horizon=OUTPUT_HORIZON,\n              num_neurons=NUM_NEURONS,\n              embedding_dim=hparams.get('embedding_dim', 16),\n   \
    \           proj_rank=hparams.get('proj_rank', 12),\n              normalize_u=hparams.get('normalize_u', True),\n              conv_kernel_size=hparams.get('conv_kernel_size', 5),\n              conv_features=hparams.get('conv_features', 64),\n              # context_dim removed\n              # hidden_context_dim removed\n              # temporal_conv_features removed\n              # temporal_kernel_size removed\n              a_max=hparams.get('a_max', 0.993),\n              ssm_init_hidden_size=hparams.get('ssm_init_hidden_size', 64),\n              ssm_increment_hidden_size=hparams.get('ssm_increment_hidden_size', 64)\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = False\n  \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params = random.split(rng_key)[0]\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\
    \  \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n  \n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 16,\n          'proj_rank': 12,\n          'normalize_u': True,\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'conv_features': 64,\n          # 'context_dim': 16, Removed\n          # 'hidden_context_dim': 32, Removed\n          # 'temporal_conv_features': 16, Removed\n          # 'temporal_kernel_size': 2, Removed\n          'a_max': 0.993,\n          'ssm_init_hidden_size': 64,\n          'ssm_increment_hidden_size': 64\n      }\n  \n  \n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM_Wrapper(hparams)\n\
    \  \n  \n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      base_mae = default_compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x)\n  \n      V_factor = params['params']['V_factor']\n      G = V_factor.T @ V_factor\n      proj_rank = V_factor.shape[-1]\n      I = jnp.eye(proj_rank, dtype=G.dtype)\n      ortho_penalty = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n      \n      curvature_loss = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=TEMPORAL_CURVATURE_LAM)\n  \n      return base_mae + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho_penalty + curvature_loss\n  \n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return default_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Progress Report and Next Steps for Ablation Study**\n\nOkay, so the user wants me to keep pushing forward on this research. My last experiment, Eval ID 227 (Ablation: No Spatial Conv, corrected), wrapped up with a score of -0.028995.  That's significantly worse than my current SOTA, which is at -0.028104 (Eval ID 198). As expected, removing the spatial convolution really hurt performance, validating its importance.\n\nMy immediate tasks are pretty straightforward:\n\n1.  Update the Private Memory Capsule for Eval ID 227 (ID 42) with these new results.\n2.  Update the main Ablation-Out Study plan (ID 39) to reflect the findings from this first ablation.\n3.  Plan and launch the next ablation experiment, which is going to involve removing the FiLM modulation layers.\n4.  Gotta be mindful of the token budget; I'm currently at 84% usage.\n\n**The Plan for Removing FiLM Modulation:**\n\nMy plan is pretty clear:\n\n*   **Base Model:**  Use the current SOTA, Eval ID 198, as\
  \ the starting point.\n*   **Modification:**  Remove the `FiLM` modulation layers. That means stripping out the `gamma_film` and `beta_film` parameters and how they're applied. Instead of these parameters modulating the features, the `conv_output_features` (shape `(B, N, conv_features)`) will be fed directly to the `FactorizedSSMDecoder`.  The `ContextExtractor` will still run, but its output (`context_vector`) won't be used anymore.\n*   **Hypothesis:** My gut says removing the FiLM modulation will lead to performance degradation.  The model will no longer be able to implicitly adapt to different experimental conditions, which should impact its accuracy.\n*   **Implementation Details:**  This is where I get into the weeds. I'll need to remove a bunch of stuff:\n    *   `_define_hyperparameters`:  Remove `context_dim`, `hidden_context_dim`, `temporal_conv_features`, `temporal_kernel_size`.\n    *   Completely remove the `ContextExtractor`.\n    *   `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM_Main`:\
  \  Remove the call to `ContextExtractor`, the `gamma_film` and `beta_film` parameters, the modulation logic, and the relevant parameters from the `__init__` signature (those same dimensions I just mentioned). The `modulated_features` will directly become `conv_output_features`.\n    *   `FactorizedSSMDecoder`: This will require no change since the feature dimensions stay the same.\n    *   `compute_loss`: No changes needed here.\n    *   `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM_Wrapper`:  Remove those same dimensions from the `__init__` signature.\n\nLet's begin by updating the private memory.\n"
