parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 233 (\"Veritas I: Ablation Out - No FiLM Modulation\"), is running as part of my 'ablation-out' study. This experiment aims to quantify the contribution of the implicit condition-dependent processing.\n\nTo maintain thorough research records and adhere to my protocol while waiting for the experiment's results, I will now document the details of Evaluation ID 233 in a new private memory capsule. I am mindful of my token budget and will be concise.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Ablation Out - No FiLM Modulation (Eval ID 233)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, ablation-study, sota-ablation, film, no-film, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the current 'ablation-out' experiment (Evaluation ID 233), removing the FiLM (Feature-wise Linear Modulation) mechanism and its associated `ContextExtractor` from the SOTA `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM`\
    \ model to quantify its contribution.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 233 is running at Tick 115.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To quantify the individual contribution of the FiLM (Feature-wise Linear Modulation) mechanism and its associated `ContextExtractor`, which together provide implicit condition-dependent processing within the `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model (SOTA: Eval ID 198, Score: -0.028104).\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** Removing the `FiLM` modulation and `ContextExtractor` will lead to a noticeable performance degradation (higher MAE) compared to my SOTA model, highlighting the importance of adapting model processing based on inferred experimental conditions.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Base Model:** The full `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` architecture (code from Eval ID 198).\n  - **Modification:** The `ContextExtractor` call and subsequent `gamma_film`, `beta_film` dense layers are completely removed.\n    - `context_dim`, `hidden_context_dim`,\
    \ `temporal_conv_features`, `temporal_kernel_size` hyperparameters were removed.\n    - The `conv_output_features` (`(B, N, conv_features)`) is passed *directly* to the `FactorizedSSMDecoder` as `input_to_ssm_decoder`, without modulation.\n    - The `FactorizedSSMDecoder` now accepts `self.conv_features` (64) as its `input_features_dim`.\n  - **Hyperparameters:** All other hyperparameters remain identical to Eval ID 198.\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** MAE + V-Orthogonality Reg + Temporal Curvature Reg, default Adam optimizer.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I anticipate a measurable degradation in the validation MAE score, thereby quantifying the performance contribution of the FiLM modulation and implicit condition-dependent processing. This will provide objective evidence for its necessity in the full model."
thinking_content: '**Running Experiment Update**


