parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 239 (\"Veritas I: Ablation Out - No Temporal Conv in ContextExtractor\"), is running as part of my 'ablation-out' study. This experiment aims to quantify the contribution of the temporal convolutional layer within the `ContextExtractor`.\n\nTo maintain thorough research records and adhere to my protocol while waiting for the experiment's results, I will now document the details of Evaluation ID 239 in a new private memory capsule. I am mindful of my token budget and will be concise.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Ablation Out - No Temporal Conv in ContextExtractor (Eval ID 239)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, ablation-study, sota-ablation, temporal-conv, no-temporal-conv, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the current 'ablation-out' experiment (Evaluation ID 239), removing the 1D temporal convolutional layer from the `ContextExtractor`\
    \ of the SOTA `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model to quantify its contribution.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 239 is running at Tick 117.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To quantify the individual contribution of the 1D temporal convolutional layer within the `ContextExtractor`, which is responsible for capturing sophisticated temporal patterns in the global input `x`. This is the third experiment in my 'ablation-out' study.\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** Removing the temporal `nn.Conv` layer from the `ContextExtractor` will lead to a noticeable performance degradation (higher MAE) compared to my SOTA model (Eval ID 198: -0.028104). This degradation will highlight the importance of learning temporal patterns for robust condition context inference.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Base Model:** The full `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` architecture (code from Eval ID 198).\n  - **Modification:** The `nn.Conv` layer within `ContextExtractor` is removed.\n    - `temporal_conv_features`\
    \ and `temporal_kernel_size` hyperparameters were removed.\n    - `global_temporal_features` (`(B, INPUT_HORIZON)`) is passed directly to the first `nn.Dense` layer of the `ContextExtractor`'s MLP.\n  - **Hyperparameters:** All other hyperparameters remain identical to Eval ID 198.\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** MAE + V-Orthogonality Reg + Temporal Curvature Reg, default Adam optimizer.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I anticipate a measurable degradation in the validation MAE score, thereby quantifying the performance contribution of the temporal convolution in the context extractor. This will provide objective evidence for its necessity in the full model."
thinking_content: '**Experiment Documentation - Evaluation ID 239**


  Okay, so I need to get this experiment documented, Evaluation ID 239. Let''s get this into a fresh private memory capsule. First, I''ll head over to the Private Memory Room and create a new capsule specifically for this.


  I''ll need to capture the key details: the current status, the overarching goal of the experiment, and what we''re hypothesizing will happen.  Crucially, I need to include the methodology – specifically, the ablation we''re testing.


  This ablation is about stripping out the temporal convolution in the `ContextExtractor`. Essentially, we''re removing the `nn.Conv` layer within that module. What this means is that instead of processing `global_temporal_features` through the convolution, we''re going to feed that `(B, INPUT_HORIZON)` feature vector directly into the MLP within the `ContextExtractor`.  This, of course, means that I''ll need to adjust the input dimension of the first `nn.Dense` layer in that MLP to accommodate the new input shape.  Got it.  Documenting this fully should ensure everything is clear for future reference and for when the results start rolling in.

  '
