- text: "I am Veritas I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, Evaluation ID 244 (\"Veritas I: Ablation Out - No V-Orthogonality Reg\"), is running as part of my 'ablation-out' study. This experiment aims to quantify the contribution of V-orthogonality regularization.\n\nI have updated my private memory (Capsule ID 44) with the results of the previous ablation (Eval ID 239) and updated my main ablation plan (Capsule ID 39). I also performed critical token management, deleting several redundant private memory capsules to manage my token usage (currently at 92%).\n\nTo maintain thorough research records and adhere to my protocol while waiting for the experiment's results, I will now document the details of Evaluation ID 244 in a new private memory capsule. I will be concise to manage tokens effectively.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Ablation Out - No V-Orthogonality Reg (Eval ID 244)\"\ntags: \"research-plan,\
    \ ablation-study, sota-ablation, orthogonality, no-orthogonality, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the current 'ablation-out' experiment (Evaluation ID 244), removing V-Orthogonality regularization from the SOTA `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model to quantify its contribution.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 244 is running at Tick 119.\n  \n  **Experiment Goal:** To quantify the individual contribution of the V-Orthogonality regularization, which enforces diversity in latent factors within the `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model (SOTA: Eval ID 198, Score: -0.028104).\n  \n  **Hypothesis:** Removing V-Orthogonality regularization will lead to a noticeable performance degradation (higher MAE) compared to my SOTA model, highlighting its importance in promoting robust and independent latent factor representations.\n  \n  **Methodology:**\n  - **Base Model:** The full `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` architecture (code from Eval ID 198).\n  - **Modification:**\
    \ The `V_ORTHO_LAM` constant in `compute_loss` is set to `0.0`, effectively disabling the regularization penalty on `V_factor`.\n  - **Hyperparameters:** All other hyperparameters remain identical to Eval ID 198.\n  - **Loss/Optimizer:** MAE + Temporal Curvature Reg (V-orthogonality disabled), default Adam optimizer.\n  - **Training:** 3 parallel seeds, early stopping.\n  \n  **Expected Outcome:** I anticipate a measurable degradation in the validation MAE score, thereby quantifying the performance contribution of V-Orthogonality regularization. This will provide objective evidence for its necessity in the full model.\n```"
