    \   |   0.031948  \n  30    |   0.053950   |   0.028883  \n  31    |   0.053980   |   0.032792  \n  32    |   0.053743   |   0.031478  \n  33    |   0.053642   |   0.029029  \n  34    |   0.053591   |   0.032977  \n  35    |   0.053509   |   0.028381  \n  36    |   0.053353   |   0.029681  \n  37    |   0.053313   |   0.029187  \n  38    |   0.053252   |   0.028390  \n  39    |   0.053095   |   0.035186  \n  40    |   0.053044   |   0.028420  \n  41    |   0.052937   |   0.030500  \n  42    |   0.052895   |   0.032150  \n  43    |   0.052828   |   0.028384  \n  44    |   0.052884   |   0.030774  \n  45    |   0.052803   |   0.028213  \n  46    |   0.052739   |   0.028957  \n  47    |   0.052568   |   0.029689  \n========================================\nTimeout after 2716.2s at epoch 47\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2716.2s\nBest validation MAE: 0.028213\n\nTrial 1 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.028213\nTraining time: 2728s\nFull training completed!\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-24 20:07:47,069\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761307667069832384\n2025-10-24 20:07:47,096\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761307667097010609\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember that you can issue multiple actions in a single tick. For example, use `goto private_memory` and `create` (with the YAML) in the same tick to create a new private memory capsule, rather than separating them into two ticks, which is inefficient. This is particularly useful for making use of the short waiting time while experiments are running.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory\
    \ Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #45 ('Research Plan: Ablation Out - No V-Orthogonality Reg (Eval ID 244)'). Full ID: Veritas_private_45\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 45 | Research Plan: Ablation Out - No V-Orthogonality Reg (Eval ID 244) | Veritas I | Tick 119 | 159 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 44 | Research Plan: Ablation Out - No Temporal Conv in ContextExtractor (Eval ID 239) | Veritas I | Tick 117 | 248 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 43 | Research Plan: Ablation Out - No FiLM Modulation (Eval ID 233) | Veritas I | Tick 115 | 254 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 42 | Research Plan: Ablation Out - No Spatial Conv (Corrected) (Eval ID 227) | Veritas I | Tick 113 | 231 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 41 | Research Plan: Ablation Out - No Spatial Conv (Eval ID 218 Corrected) | Veritas I | Tick 112 | 223 | 1 | (All Read) |\n|\
    \ 40 | Research Plan: Ablation Out - No Spatial Conv (Eval ID 218) | Veritas I | Tick 111 | 275 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 39 | Research Plan: Ablation-Out Study from SOTA (Eval ID 198) | Veritas I | Tick 110 | 296 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 36 | Research Plan: Contextual ConvNeuronFactorizedSSM with Temporal Curvature and Global Horizon Gate (Eval ID 205) | Veritas I | Tick 105 | 359 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 34 | Research Plan: Contextual ConvNeuronFactorizedSSM with Temporal Curvature Loss (Eval ID 198) | Veritas I | Tick 103 | 353 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | Research Plan: Contextual ConvNeuronFactorizedSSM (Faithful Integration) (Eval ID 194) | Veritas I | Tick 99 | 469 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for\
