    \ ssm, global-horizon-gate, re-attempt, ZAPBench\"\nabstract: \"Documentation of the current experiment (Evaluation ID 257), a re-attempt to integrate Ariadne I's `Global Horizon Gate (gamma)` for dynamic temporal weighting into the `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Current Status:** Evaluation ID 257 is running at Tick 125.\n  **Experiment Goal:** Re-integrate Ariadne I's `Global Horizon Gate (gamma)` into the `ContextualConvNeuronFactorizedSSM` model (SOTA: Eval ID 198, Score -0.028104) to refine temporal dynamics.\n  **Hypothesis:** The `gamma` gate will dynamically adjust SSM output influence over the prediction horizon, optimizing short-term vs. long-term accuracy, and potentially improving SOTA. Previous attempt (Eval ID 205) regressed; this re-attempt seeks to establish positive impact on a stable base.\n  **Methodology:** Base model from Eval ID 198. `FactorizedSSMDecoder` modified to include `gamma_start=0.25`, `gamma_end=0.99`. All other hyperparameters/losses\
